      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "@{5f4773dac246b672791386d7|full_name}: \nIn such a case, when using Dynamic Bone, I think that it has been fixed by stiffness.\nIf you didn't use stiffness, the bones would have moved.\nI have prepared a demonstration movie.\nhttps://twitter.com/takec_vrc/status/1500491182048428038\nMy suggestion is closer to the behavior of Dynamic Bone so I think the conversion will work better.\nIf you don't want to move it, you can fix it using immobile as before.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
